+# Documentation
+
+Project documentation for `buddy`, a mobile-first, offline-capable PWA virtual
+pet game.
+
+## Contents
+
+| Path | Description |
+|---|---|
+| `buddy/reports/phases/` | Phase completion reports and phase audits (12 files). |
+| `prompts/buddy_virtual_pet_v2_complete_prompt_pack/` | Vendored planning/prompt pack (87 files). See provenance below. |
+
+## Prompt pack provenance
+
+`docs/prompts/buddy_virtual_pet_v2_complete_prompt_pack/` is a large planning
+and prompt pack (87 markdown files across `prompts/`, `specs/`, `content/`,
+`ux/`, `integration/`, `audits/`, `checklists/`, `templates/`, and `runner/`)
+committed alongside the application.
+
+- **Role:** planning/specification material only; it contains no runnable
+  product code.
+- **Authorship / ownership:** not recorded in-repo and therefore **unconfirmed**
+  (finding `SUPPLY-P2-003`). It must not be assumed to be third-party or
+  in-house until the maintainer/legal owner confirms it.
+- **Licensing:** unconfirmed. Treat as all-rights-reserved pending confirmation;
+  do not redistribute the pack outside the organization.
+- **Originality constraint:** the pack's own `README.md` (line 17) states that
+  Tamaweb, Tamagotchi, and other copyrighted/proprietary projects must not be
+  copied, and the application code must be original.
+
+This classification is tracked under finding `SUPPLY-P2-003` in audit run
+`20261003-0018-master-99abf29`.
+
+## Licensing
+
+The repository has no chosen license yet; `LICENSE` records the pending,
+all-rights-reserved status and the target-license decision is an open question
+under finding `SUPPLY-P1-001`. See also the root `NOTICE`.
